<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
  <meta charset="UTF-8">
  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
  <title>Ziva — Basic Web URL Phishing Detector</title>
  <meta name="description" content="Ziva is a pure static rule-based phishing link analyzer. Check before you click.">
  <link rel="stylesheet" href="/static/style.css">
</head>
<body>
  <!-- Skip link for keyboard accessibility -->
  <a href="#analyzer-input" class="skip-link">Skip to URL analyzer</a>

  <!-- Header -->
  <header class="app-header">
    <div class="container header-inner">
      <div class="brand">
        <!-- Inline SVG Shield / Link Check Logo -->
        <svg class="brand-logo" width="34" height="34" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M12 2L3 6V11C3 16.55 6.84 21.74 12 23C17.16 21.74 21 16.55 21 11V6L12 2Z" fill="#0a0a0a" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
          <path d="M9 11.5L11 13.5L15 9.5" stroke="#ef4444" stroke-width="2.5" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"/>
        </svg>
        <div class="brand-text">
          <h1 class="brand-name">Ziva</h1>
          <p class="brand-tagline">Check before you click.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="header-actions">
        <a href="/api/docs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm">API Docs</a>
        <button id="theme-toggle" class="btn btn-icon" aria-label="Toggle light and dark mode" title="Toggle theme">
          <svg id="theme-icon-dark" class="icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <path d="M21 12.79A9 9 0 1 1 11.21 3 7 7 0 0 0 21 12.79z"></path>
          </svg>
          <svg id="theme-icon-light" class="icon hidden" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="5"></circle>
            <line x1="12" y1="1" x2="12" y2="3"></line>
            <line x1="12" y1="21" x2="12" y2="23"></line>
            <line x1="4.22" y1="4.22" x2="5.64" y2="5.64"></line>
            <line x1="18.36" y1="18.36" x2="19.78" y2="19.78"></line>
            <line x1="1" y1="12" x2="3" y2="12"></line>
            <line x1="21" y1="12" x2="23" y2="12"></line>
            <line x1="4.22" y1="19.78" x2="5.64" y2="18.36"></line>
            <line x1="18.36" y1="5.64" x2="19.78" y2="4.22"></line>
          </svg>
        </button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="container main-content">
    <!-- Notice Banner -->
    <div class="guarantee-banner" role="status">
      <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
        <rect x="3" y="11" width="18" height="11" rx="2" ry="2"></rect>
        <path d="M7 11V7a5 5 0 0 1 10 0v4"></path>
      </svg>
      <span><strong>Pure Static Analysis:</strong> Ziva never fetches, visits, or resolves the submitted URL. Your analysis is 100% offline and confidential.</span>
    </div>

    <!-- URL Analyzer Form Section -->
    <section class="card analyzer-card" aria-labelledby="analyzer-heading">
      <h2 id="analyzer-heading" class="sr-only">URL Security Analyzer</h2>
      
      <form id="analyze-form" class="analyze-form" novalidate>
        <label for="analyzer-input" class="form-label">
          Paste a suspicious link to inspect
        </label>
        
        <div class="input-group">
          <span class="input-prefix-icon" aria-hidden="true">
            <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2">
              <path d="M10 13a5 5 0 0 0 7.54.54l3-3a5 5 0 0 0-7.07-7.07l-1.72 1.71"></path>
              <path d="M14 11a5 5 0 0 0-7.54-.54l-3 3a5 5 0 0 0 7.07 7.07l1.71-1.71"></path>
            </svg>
          </span>
          <input
            type="text"
            id="analyzer-input"
            class="url-input"
            placeholder="e.g. paypal-verify-account-login.example or https://google.com@evil.com"
            autocomplete="off"
            spellcheck="false"
            required
            maxlength="2048"
          >
          <button type="button" id="clear-input-btn" class="btn-clear hidden" aria-label="Clear input field" title="Clear">
            &times;
          </button>
          <button type="submit" id="analyze-btn" class="btn btn-primary">
            <span class="btn-text">Analyze URL</span>
            <span class="btn-loader hidden" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          </button>
        </div>

        <div id="input-error" class="input-error-msg hidden" role="alert"></div>
      </form>

      <!-- Quick Example Buttons -->
      <div class="examples-bar">
        <span class="examples-label">Try an example:</span>
        <div class="example-buttons">
          <button type="button" class="btn-chip chip-danger" data-url="https://paypal-verify-account-login.example">
            Phishing Hyphens
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="btn-chip chip-danger" data-url="https://google.com@evil.com/auth">
            @ Spoof Trick
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="btn-chip chip-warning" data-url="http://paypal.com.evil.xyz">
            Brand Subdomain
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="btn-chip chip-warning" data-url="http://0xC0A80001/login">
            Hex IP Address
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="btn-chip chip-warning" data-url="https://xn--pypal-4ve.com">
            Punycode Homograph
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="btn-chip chip-safe" data-url="https://github.com">
            Safe (GitHub)
          </button>
          <button type="button" class="btn-chip chip-safe" data-url="https://www.wikipedia.org">
            Safe (Wikipedia)
          </button>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- ARIA Live Announcement Region -->
    <div id="live-region" class="sr-only" aria-live="polite" aria-atomic="true"></div>

    <!-- Results Container -->
    <section id="results-section" class="results-container hidden" aria-labelledby="results-heading">
      <div class="card result-main-card">
        <div class="result-header">
          <div>
            <span class="sub-title">Inspection Results</span>
            <h2 id="results-heading" class="result-title">URL Safety Verdict</h2>
          </div>
          <div id="verdict-badge" class="verdict-badge" aria-label="Safety Verdict">
            <!-- Populated via JS: Safe / Suspicious / High Risk -->
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Defanged URL display -->
        <div class="defanged-box">
          <span class="defanged-label">Analyzed URL (Defanged):</span>
          <code id="display-url" class="defanged-text"></code>
        </div>

        <!-- Score Gauge & Overview -->
        <div class="score-grid">
          <div class="score-card">
            <div class="score-circle-wrapper">
              <svg class="score-gauge" width="160" height="160" viewBox="0 0 160 160">
                <circle class="gauge-bg" cx="80" cy="80" r="68" />
                <circle id="gauge-fill" class="gauge-fill" cx="80" cy="80" r="68" />
              </svg>
              <div class="score-number-overlay">
                <span id="score-value" class="score-big">0</span>
                <span class="score-max">/ 100</span>
                <span class="score-label">Risk Score</span>
              </div>
            </div>
            
            <div class="scale-legend">
              <div class="scale-item"><span class="scale-dot dot-safe"></span> 0–24 Safe</div>
              <div class="scale-item"><span class="scale-dot dot-warn"></span> 25–59 Suspicious</div>
              <div class="scale-item"><span class="scale-dot dot-danger"></span> 60+ High Risk</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="verdict-summary-card">
            <h3 id="verdict-summary-title" class="summary-title">Summary</h3>
            <p id="verdict-summary-text" class="summary-text"></p>
            
            <div class="safe-caveat-alert" id="safe-caveat-box">
              <svg width="18" height="18" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
                <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle>
                <line x1="12" y1="8" x2="12" y2="12"></line>
                <line x1="12" y1="16" x2="12.01" y2="16"></line>
              </svg>
              <span><strong>Note:</strong> A "Safe" score means no known static heuristics or structural red flags were triggered. It is <em>not an absolute guarantee</em> that the destination is harmless.</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- URL Breakdown Section -->
        <div class="url-breakdown-section">
          <h3 class="breakdown-title">
            <span>URL Anatomy Breakdown</span>
            <span class="breakdown-subtitle">Visual deconstruction to help you identify spoofed parts</span>
          </h3>

          <div class="breakdown-visual" id="breakdown-visual-chips">
            <!-- Populated via script: scheme, subdomains, registered_domain, tld, port, path -->
          </div>

          <div class="breakdown-table-wrapper">
            <table class="breakdown-table">
              <thead>
                <tr>
                  <th scope="col">Component</th>
                  <th scope="col">Extracted Value</th>
                  <th scope="col">Security Significance</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody id="breakdown-table-body">
                <!-- Populated via JS -->
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Findings List -->
        <div class="findings-section">
          <h3 class="findings-heading">
            <span>Detection Findings</span>
            <span id="findings-count-badge" class="count-badge">0 findings</span>
          </h3>

          <div id="findings-list" class="findings-list">
            <!-- Populated via JS -->
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Recent History Section -->
    <section class="card history-card" aria-labelledby="history-heading">
      <div class="history-header">
        <div class="history-title-wrap">
          <svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
            <circle cx="12" cy="12" r="10"></circle>
            <polyline points="12 6 12 12 16 14"></polyline>
          </svg>
          <h2 id="history-heading" class="section-title">Recent Checks</h2>
          <span class="history-badge" id="history-count">0 / 10</span>
        </div>
        <button type="button" id="clear-history-btn" class="btn btn-outline btn-sm">Clear History</button>
      </div>

      <div id="history-empty" class="history-empty">
        <p>No recent URL checks yet. Analyze any URL above to build your session history.</p>
      </div>

      <div id="history-list" class="history-list hidden">
        <!-- History items inserted via JS -->
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Educational Section: How to spot phishing links -->
    <section class="card educational-card" aria-labelledby="edu-heading">
      <div class="edu-header">
        <svg width="24" height="24" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="#dc2626" stroke-width="2" aria-hidden="true">
          <path d="M2 3h6a4 4 0 0 1 4 4v14a3 3 0 0 0-3-3H2z"></path>
          <path d="M22 3h-6a4 4 0 0 0-4 4v14a3 3 0 0 1 3-3h7z"></path>
        </svg>
        <h2 id="edu-heading" class="section-title">How to Spot Phishing Links</h2>
      </div>
      <p class="edu-intro">
        Cybercriminals rely on subtle visual deception to trick you into entering credentials on lookalike websites.
        Here are five cardinal rules to keep in mind:
      </p>

      <div class="tips-grid">
        <div class="tip-card">
          <div class="tip-badge">1</div>
          <h3 class="tip-title">Inspect the Registered Domain</h3>
          <p class="tip-desc">
            In <code>paypal.com.evil.xyz</code>, the actual destination is <strong>evil.xyz</strong>, NOT PayPal.
            Always read from right to left before the first slash to identify who truly owns the site.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="tip-card">
          <div class="tip-badge">2</div>
          <h3 class="tip-title">Watch Out for the "@" Trick</h3>
          <p class="tip-desc">
            URLs like <code>https://google.com@attacker.com</code> send your browser directly to <strong>attacker.com</strong>.
            Everything preceding the <code>@</code> symbol is treated as user credentials and discarded.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="tip-card">
          <div class="tip-badge">3</div>
          <h3 class="tip-title">Beware of Hyphen Stacking</h3>
          <p class="tip-desc">
            Legitimate services rarely use names like <code>chase-security-verify-login.com</code>.
            Excessive hyphens joining brand names with urgency terms are a hallmark indicator of phishing.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="tip-card">
          <div class="tip-badge">4</div>
          <h3 class="tip-title">Look Out for Homographs</h3>
          <p class="tip-desc">
            Non-Latin characters from the Cyrillic or Greek alphabets (e.g., Cyrillic <em>а</em> vs Latin <em>a</em>) can produce identical-looking addresses (Punycode <code>xn--</code>). Check the decoded address carefully.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="tip-card">
          <div class="tip-badge">5</div>
          <h3 class="tip-title">Never Rely Solely on HTTPS</h3>
          <p class="tip-desc">
            A padlock icon only means the connection is encrypted; it does <strong>not</strong> mean the website is legitimate.
            Over 80% of modern phishing sites obtain free SSL certificates.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="tip-card">
          <div class="tip-badge">6</div>
          <h3 class="tip-title">Raw IP Addresses Are Suspicious</h3>
          <p class="tip-desc">
            Public consumer portals do not host customer login pages on bare numeric IP addresses (like <code>http://192.168.1.1</code> or hex codes). If there is no domain name, proceed with extreme caution.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <!-- Footer -->
  <footer class="app-footer">
    <div class="container footer-inner">
      <div class="footer-brand">
        <strong>Ziva</strong> — Static URL Phishing Detector. "Check before you click."
      </div>
      <div class="footer-note">
        Educational heuristic tool. Does not contact, visit, or resolve target URLs.
      </div>
    </div>
  </footer>

  <script src="/static/script.js"></script>
<script src="https://cdn.raccoonai.tech/packages/branding-badge.js?v=7" defer></script></body>
</html>
